# Settings for running Pince on your own computer. Every one is optional.
# Copy this file to `.env`, remove the `# ` in front of the settings you need and give them values.
# `npm start` reads `.env` by itself; `npm run doctor` shows what it picked up, by name only.
# `.env` is ignored by git. Never put real values in this example file.
# docs/CONFIGURATION.md explains each setting.

# Local server
# PORT=46173
# LIBRARY_LOCAL_DIR=.library

# Account names (defaults: parinte, copil). Passwords are generated on the first run
# and saved in .library/local-access.json unless you set them here.
# PARENT_USERNAME=
# CHILD_USERNAME=
# BOOTSTRAP_PARENT_PASSWORD=
# BOOTSTRAP_CHILD_PASSWORD=

# The keys below can also be added in the browser, where each one is checked first: in the set-up
# screen on the first start, or under Family settings. A value set here wins over one saved there.

# Photo recognition (Azure OpenAI). Without these, books are added by typing or with an uploaded cover.
# AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=
# AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT=
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Text detection (Azure AI Vision). Places title and cover cut-outs in scanned photos.
# AZURE_VISION_ENDPOINT=
# AZURE_VISION_KEY=

# Cover and catalogue lookups
# GOOGLE_BOOKS_API_KEY=
# BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY=

# Cost estimates shown to the parent
# AZURE_MONTHLY_RESERVE_USD=
# TAX_MULTIPLIER=
